  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nFor the weekend, high pressure to the east will strengthen while a\ntrough of low pressure off the California coast maintains drier\nsouthwest flow aloft. For early next week, there are some\ndifferences in the placement of low pressure near or farther off\nthe California coast with greater spread in the high temperature\nguidance. Cluster analysis shows the model solutions that are\ncooler are those with the low pressure along the California coast\nversus farther off the coast with those solutions with low\npressure near the coast representing around 20 percent of \nensemble solutions.\n\nHigh temperatures will slowly warm for Saturday through Tuesday.\nHigh temperatures on Saturday will range from around average near\nthe coast to 4 to 8 degrees below average for the mountains and\ninland valleys. For next Tuesday, high temperatures will range\nfrom around average near the coast to around 5 degrees below\naverage for the mountains and inland valleys with the lower\ndeserts a few degrees above average for the lower deserts.\n\nHigh temperatures on Saturday will range from the 70s near the\ncoast to the mid 80s to mid 90s for the Inland Empire with 100 to\n104 for the lower deserts. For next Tuesday, high temperatures\nwill range from the 70s near the coast to the 90s in the Inland\nEmpire with 106 to 110 for the lower deserts.",
